    - No MCP execution path and no restart/reopen lifecycle step are part of v4.
    
    ## Parallel Agent OS
    
    When `hostAction=PREPARE_NATIVE_SUBAGENTS`, run `executionkit agents run .` (add `--boost` when requested). When `hostAction=SPAWN_NATIVE_SUBAGENTS`, spawn one worker per delegation in its isolated worktree.
    
    Workers open `.executionkit/agent-claim.json`, read only the exact `taskRef`, lazily load routed resources and modify only owned surfaces. They never mutate canonical TODO/control state. The orchestrator alone collects, integrates, cleans claims and updates canonical task state.
    
    ## Boundary and release truth
    
    - Task: implementation + changed-file integrity checks + State checkpoint; no automatic full Test/Audit.
    - Wave: `executionkit boundary wave .`.
    - Phase: `executionkit boundary phase .`.
    - Release: exact-candidate release gates; production deployment only through Launch OS.
    - CI is manual self-hosted only; no GitHub-hosted minutes or automatic push/PR runs.
    - A tag/version string is not a release. Publication requires exact-candidate evidence and a verified real GitHub Release object.
    
